{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Q88QfY3ZtpxTuDpN4bPUK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines review form\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FAQ - EMNLP 2026\",\"url\":\"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N\",\"url\":\"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026\"},{\"title\":\"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)\",\"url\":\"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://www.ecnlpir.org/reviewerguidelines.html\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...\",\"url\":\"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and the review process. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review System\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Requirements\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nACL has adopted a policy requiring all authors to sign up as reviewers, with assignments made based on their qualifications. Reviewers who fail to fulfill their responsibilities may become ineligible to commit or (re-)submit papers in the following ARR cycle.\n\n## Key Deadlines\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\n## Finding the Official Review Form\n\nFor the specific EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines and review form, you would likely need to access the official ARR (ACL Rolling Review) platform at **aclrollingreview.org** or the EMNLP 2026 official website at **2026.emnlp.org**. The search results reference these platforms but don't contain the direct link to the specific review form document for Findings submissions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a034fb2-c99a-4077-810e-027f0ae362c6","uuid":"8f1a3dd0-c5ad-4416-ae17-fca3c4872bab","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:05:51.962Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines review form","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015gs9AqQ6fn8TTxs9VAwRvb","content":[{"title":"FAQ - EMNLP 2026","url":"https://2026.emnlp.org/faq/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 : The 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in N","url":"https://callforpaper.org/call-for-papers-emnlp-2026"},{"title":"LINGUIST List 37.972 Confs: 2026 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing (Hungary)","url":"https://linguistlist.org/issues/37/972/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines","url":"https://www.ecnlpir.org/reviewerguidelines.html"},{"title":"EMNLP 2026 | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2026"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP: Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing 2027 2026 2025 ...","url":"http://www.wikicfp.com/cfp/program?id=883"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"Based on the search results, I found information about EMNLP 2026 reviewer guidelines and the review process. Here's what I found:\n\n## EMNLP 2026 Review System\n\nEMNLP 2026 will use ACL Rolling Review (ARR) as a reviewing system, but final decisions will be made by the conference.\n\n## Reviewer Guidelines and Requirements\n\nAll reviewers must familiarize themselves with the latest version of the ARR reviewer guidelines and perform the reviews on time and in line with ARR requirements.\n\nACL has adopted a policy requiring all authors to sign up as reviewers, with assignments made based on their qualifications. Reviewers who fail to fulfill their responsibilities may become ineligible to commit or (re-)submit papers in the following ARR cycle.\n\n## Key Deadlines\n\nIf you receive assignments, your reviews must be completed by July 6, or your meta-reviews - by July 29.\n\n## Finding the Official Review Form\n\nFor the specific EMNLP 2026 Findings reviewer guidelines and review form, you would likely need to access the official ARR (ACL Rolling Review) platform at **aclrollingreview.org** or the EMNLP 2026 official website at **2026.emnlp.org**. The search results reference these platforms but don't contain the direct link to the specific review form document for Findings submissions."],"durationSeconds":8.825494951000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dfdfuh7SuryY313zSyMusW","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025\",\"url\":\"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\"},{\"title\":\"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025\"},{\"title\":\"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/\"},{\"title\":\"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation\"},{\"title\":\"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters\"},{\"title\":\"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬\",\"url\":\"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020\",\"url\":\"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric:\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections. The In-Depth Review section is for giving your overall assessment of the paper and providing evidence to support your opinions, with the core review being the most important part that should include your view of the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds at making these contributions.\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nA 5 point scale with half point increments is used, with detailed explanations for each point level provided in the review form. A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers should try to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, but if it is indeed a borderline paper or if you are unable to decide, you should use 3.\n\n## Review Form Subsections\n\nThe core review should include your view of the main contributions, significant strong and weak parts, and can be a 2 paragraph or longer essay with bullet points, describing how the work advances the state of knowledge in computational linguistics. The form includes a \"Reasons to accept\" subsection that briefly summarizes the main reasons why the paper should be accepted.\n\n## Reproducibility Assessment\n\nIn the review form, reviewers answer the question \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5, with detailed explanations for each point level provided in the review form. Reviewers also answer whether the authors' answers to the Reproducibility Checklist are useful, with three choices provided (very useful, somewhat useful, not useful).\n\nFor the complete review form details and specific scoring rubric descriptions, you can access the official EMNLP 2025 reviewer instructions at: https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a034fb2-c99a-4077-810e-027f0ae362c6","uuid":"f3e7fab7-9022-4fed-9b11-764d03bb53e5","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:05:53.055Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines scoring rubric review form criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011TzwkHWY69qEuRyEi15RJx","content":[{"title":"NAACL-HLT 2021 Instructions for Reviewers - EMNLP 2025","url":"https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"},{"title":"Changes to reviewer volunteering requirement and incentives in May 2025 cycle (EMNLP 2025)","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/incentives2025"},{"title":"Advice on Reviewing for EMNLP","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-17-write-good-reviews/"},{"title":"EMNLP 2025 Conference | OpenReview","url":"https://openreview.net/group?id=EMNLP%2F2025%2FConference"},{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ICML 2025 Peer Review FAQ","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2025/PeerReviewFAQ"},{"title":"ACL Policies for Review and Citation - Admin Wiki","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/index.php/ACL_Policies_for_Review_and_Citation"},{"title":"[Policy Spotlight] EMNLP 2025 Criteria for “Highly Irresponsible” Reviewers — What It Means & Why It Matters | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/70/policy-spotlight-emnlp-2025-criteria-for-highly-irresponsible-reviewers-what-it-means-why-it-matters"},{"title":"‭ACL Peer Review Committee Report‬","url":"https://www.aclweb.org/adminwiki/images/d/d3/ACL_Peer_Review_Committee_Report2_Incentives_May_2025.pdf"},{"title":"Instructions for Reviewers for EMNLP 2020","url":"https://2020.emnlp.org/blog/2020-05-26-instructions-for-reviewers/"}]},"Based on the search results, here's information about EMNLP 2025 reviewer guidelines and scoring rubric:\n\n## Review Form Structure\n\nThe review form consists of four main sections. The In-Depth Review section is for giving your overall assessment of the paper and providing evidence to support your opinions, with the core review being the most important part that should include your view of the main contributions the paper intended to make and how well it succeeds at making these contributions.\n\n## Scoring Scale\n\nA 5 point scale with half point increments is used, with detailed explanations for each point level provided in the review form. A rating of 3 (ambivalent) is allowed, and reviewers should try to take a stand on whether the paper is above or below the borderline by selecting 2.5 or 3.5, but if it is indeed a borderline paper or if you are unable to decide, you should use 3.\n\n## Review Form Subsections\n\nThe core review should include your view of the main contributions, significant strong and weak parts, and can be a 2 paragraph or longer essay with bullet points, describing how the work advances the state of knowledge in computational linguistics. The form includes a \"Reasons to accept\" subsection that briefly summarizes the main reasons why the paper should be accepted.\n\n## Reproducibility Assessment\n\nIn the review form, reviewers answer the question \"How do you rate the paper's reproducibility? Will members of the ACL community be able to reproduce or verify the results in this paper?\" using scores of 1-5, with detailed explanations for each point level provided in the review form. Reviewers also answer whether the authors' answers to the Reproducibility Checklist are useful, with three choices provided (very useful, somewhat useful, not useful).\n\nFor the complete review form details and specific scoring rubric descriptions, you can access the official EMNLP 2025 reviewer instructions at: https://2025.emnlp.org/reviewer/instructions/"],"durationSeconds":9.663761311000002}}
