{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012m7yshqWPSNrkos6BJDTEZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review excitement score scale 1-5 definition \"overall assessment\" 4 3.5 3 2.5 accept reject\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found detailed information about the ACL Rolling Review excitement score scale and overall assessment definitions:\n\n## Excitement Score Scale (1-5)\n\nThe excitement scores are:\n- **5 = Highly Exciting**: \"I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n- **4 = Exciting**: \"I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n- **3 = Interesting**: \"I might mention some points of this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference if there's time.\"\n- **2 = Potentially Interesting**: \"this paper does not resonate with me, but it might with others in the *ACL community.\"\n- **1 = Not Exciting**: \"this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community\"\n\nExcitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\n\n## Overall Assessment Definition\n\nThe Overall assessment score is \"an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue.\" This is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Key Distinction\n\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a034fb2-c99a-4077-810e-027f0ae362c6","uuid":"ddfd2cd4-d28b-4969-80cf-d705c4ea1996","timestamp":"2026-05-13T17:06:19.136Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review excitement score scale 1-5 definition \"overall assessment\" 4 3.5 3 2.5 accept reject","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_015z794BmPZgLKRjKWkP9t2K","content":[{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found detailed information about the ACL Rolling Review excitement score scale and overall assessment definitions:\n\n## Excitement Score Scale (1-5)\n\nThe excitement scores are:\n- **5 = Highly Exciting**: \"I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n- **4 = Exciting**: \"I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\"\n- **3 = Interesting**: \"I might mention some points of this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference if there's time.\"\n- **2 = Potentially Interesting**: \"this paper does not resonate with me, but it might with others in the *ACL community.\"\n- **1 = Not Exciting**: \"this paper does not resonate with me, and I don't think it would with others in the *ACL community\"\n\nExcitement is subjective and does not necessarily follow what is popular in the field.\n\n## Overall Assessment Definition\n\nThe Overall assessment score is \"an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue.\" This is a composite score reflecting assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Key Distinction\n\nSometimes you may find the work sound, but not something that is interesting for you personally. Such preferences are more subjective and should be reflected in a separate excitement score, which is orthogonal to the assessment of the soundness of the paper."],"durationSeconds":6.9344965620000005}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015o38MC34ZY1qsH8A6RdLAm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the complete ARR/EMNLP review criteria. Let me summarize:\n\n**ARR Review Form (used by EMNLP 2026):**\n\n**Soundness** (1-5):\n- 5 = Excellent (one of the most thorough studies)\n- 4 = Strong (sufficient support for all claims)\n- 3 = Acceptable (sufficient support for main claims)\n- 2 = Poor (some claims not well-supported)\n\n\n- 1 = Major issues\n\n**Excitement** (1-5):\n- 5 = Highly Exciting\n- 4 = Exciting\n- 3 = Interesting\n- 2 = Potentially Interesting\n- 1 = Not Exciting\n\n**Overall Assessment** (1-5, half-point increments):\n- 5 = Consider for Award\n- 4 = Accept\n- 3.5 = Lean Accept\n- 3 = Borderline\n- 2.5 = Lean Reject\n- 2 = Resubmit next cycle\n- 1.5 = Resubmit after next cycle\n- 1 = Do not resubmit\n\nNow I have what I need to set up the review process. I'll dispatch two reviewers in parallel—one focusing on methods and experiments, the other on novelty and related work—with blind prompts that include the full paper, experimental context, and EMNLP/ARR scoring criteria. Once both return, I'll run through the roundtable discussion steps: independent assessments, cross-sharing, and synthesis.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1146,"cache_read_input_tokens":60525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1146},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2a034fb2-c99a-4077-810e-027f0ae362c6","uuid":"1aaed01d-cd0c-46c2-ad24-320dc7f35dfd"}
